tomorrow's inauguration will look a bit  different than other inaugurations in  recent years we know that  president-elect joe biden will deliver a  speech from the traditional spot at the  capitol we've seen that  but the crowds will be replaced by sea  of flags we have never seen that  then he's going to travel to arlington  national cemetery with three former  presidents  before returning for a very scaled-down  parade  chip reid looks at how inaugurations  have changed over the years  kennedy aye george herbert walker bush  it's a moment  that focuses the attention of a nation  so help me god congratulations mr  president  that exact moment when the  president-elect finishes that oath  he is the president of the united states  and the previous president  is simply a citizen presidential  historian doris kearns goodwin says that  even without the customary crowds and  galas  this inauguration like so many others  will mark a dramatic  change in direction every inauguration  is a new beginning it's almost like a  spiritual beginning  in 1933 speaking amid the great  depression  franklin delano roosevelt issued an  enduring call  for national resilience the only thing  we have to  fear is fear itself  the most important thing he said was  that there had been an absence of  national leadership and he was going to  provide  that leadership it produced a change of  mood in the country at large  do you think that joe biden is being  inaugurated at a time that at least in  some ways is similar  i think that the crisis has many  similarities the crisis provides an  opportunity for a leader to mobilize the  resources of the nation  and if the leader is up to it and if the  citizens are up to it  that is when change can really happen  the torch has been passed  to a new generation the dawning of a new  era was also  john f kennedy's central theme in 1961  more than two decades younger than his  predecessor he delivered  a memorable invitation to public  not what your country can do for you  ask what you can do for your country  there's no question that he tapped  something that was already there  and it meant that young people felt a  sense of doing something for their  country  hi ronald reagan in 1981 ronald reagan  changed the look of the modern  inauguration  directly in front of me the monument to  a monumental man  moving it from the east steps of the  capitol to the grand west front with its  stunning view  of the national mall while calling for a  major shift  in the nation's politics government is  not the solution to our problem  government is the problem and as his  defeated rival  jimmy carter looked on do you think that  president trump's decision  not to attend is genuinely harmful to  american democracy it's really important  for the  president to come to his successors  inauguration  what it symbolizes is that he's  accepting that this has happened and to  not do it  i think is really leaving a blank in  democracy  and really hurting the exercise of this  extremely  wonderful moment also missing this time  is what usually happens  behind the scenes there were visits of  the families to the white house  letters have been exchanged on the last  day of the presidency  the sense really of being a part of  welcoming the new person  into what is the people's home all of  those rituals are gone by the wayside  as a former vice president joe biden has  been part of the pageantry before  and while this event will look different  his words will still  carry historic significance what do you  think he needs to learn  from previous inaugurations all of those  great inaugural addresses were not just  the leaders saying this is what i'm  going to do  they're asking the country to respond  and i think it's that linkage that he  has to make  because that's what an inauguration is  it's a new leader taking office  but it's a citizenry that's looking  perhaps for a new beginning  the last president who refused to attend  the inauguration of his successor was  andrew johnson 152 years ago  and president trump and andrew johnson  have one other big thing in common  they are two of the three presidents to  be impeached  anthony maybe not a note in history you  want to be aligned with chip thank you  very much
 

